4. Moran duality and the 2 <-> 3 mirror of the exponent 1 - h
  ok   rho(theta) - 1 = 2^theta (g(theta) - 1)/(2^theta - 1): same zero set {1, 2} as THM-4504's Moran function
  ok   min rho = rho(theta*) = 0.946504577 = 3^-(1-h), h = H(log_3 2) = 0.949956, theta* = log2(log2 3/(log2 3 - 1)) = 1.438033
  ok   first-passage mass ~ d^-3/2 3^-(1-h)d: fitted slope -0.054987 vs -(1-h) ln 3 = -0.054979 over 877 nonzero terms d <= 1500 (the 3-adic mirror of the forward glide law W_k = Theta(2^(hk) k^(-3/2)), THM-4504)
